const NOTES=[
{id:'homophones-100',title:'100 Important Homophones — Competitive Exams',category:'Vocabulary',description:'Your original 100-set vocabulary reference, with a searchable reading view and the original PDF.',letter:'Aa',sourceLabel:'Original PDF',readingLabel:'100 sets · 2-page PDF',languageLabel:'English reference',pdf:'assets/notes/100-important-homophones.pdf',sourceFileName:'100_Important_Homophones_Competitive_Exams(1).pdf',searchTerms:HOMOPHONE_SETS.flatMap(s=>s.words.map(w=>w.word)).join(' ')},
{id:'figures-of-speech',title:'Figures of Speech Cheat Sheet',category:'Literature',minutes:5,description:'Distinguish simile, metaphor, personification and the devices exams love to mix up.',letter:'Aa',body:`<h2>Recognise the comparison</h2><p><strong>Simile</strong> makes an explicit comparison, often with <em>like</em> or <em>as</em>. <strong>Metaphor</strong> identifies one thing as another.</p><div class="example">Simile: Her smile is <strong>like sunshine</strong>.<br>Metaphor: Her smile <strong>is sunshine</strong>.</div><h2>Give life, exaggerate, or create contrast</h2><ul><li><strong>Personification:</strong> gives human qualities to something non-human. “The wind whispered.”</li><li><strong>Hyperbole:</strong> deliberate exaggeration. “I have told you a thousand times.”</li><li><strong>Oxymoron:</strong> places apparently contradictory terms together. “Deafening silence.”</li><li><strong>Paradox:</strong> a statement that seems contradictory but may express a truth. “Less is more.”</li></ul><h2>Listen to the sounds</h2><ul><li><strong>Alliteration:</strong> repetition of initial consonant sounds in nearby words. “Wild winds whistle.”</li><li><strong>Assonance:</strong> repetition of vowel sounds in nearby words. “Slow road.”</li><li><strong>Onomatopoeia:</strong> words that imitate sounds. “Buzz”, “hiss”, “clang”.</li></ul><h2>Common exam trap</h2><p>Alliteration depends on <strong>sound</strong>, rather than just repeated letters. Also, the mere presence of “like” does not make a sentence a simile: “I like tea” contains no figurative comparison.</p><div class="example" lang="kn">ಪದಗಳನ್ನು ಮಾತ್ರ ನೋಡಬೇಡಿ; ಅರ್ಥ ಮತ್ತು ಧ್ವನಿಯನ್ನು ಗಮನಿಸಿ.</div><h2>Quick check</h2><p>“The stars danced in the sky.” → <strong>Personification</strong>. Dancing is a human action attributed to stars.</p>`},
{id:'subject-verb-agreement',title:'Subject–Verb Agreement',category:'Grammar',minutes:5,description:'Find the real subject, ignore intervening phrases, and choose the correct verb.',letter:'V',body:`<h2>Start with the subject</h2><p>In the simple present, a third-person singular subject generally takes a verb with <strong>-s / -es</strong>. A plural subject takes the base form.</p><div class="example">The student <strong>reads</strong>.<br>The students <strong>read</strong>.</div><h2>Ignore the words between</h2><p>A phrase between the subject and verb does not change the subject’s number.</p><div class="example">The <strong>quality</strong> of these books <strong>is</strong> excellent.<br>“Books” is inside the prepositional phrase. The subject is “quality”.</div><h2>Frequent exam patterns</h2><ul><li><strong>Each / every:</strong> use a singular verb. “Each of the students is ready.”</li><li><strong>One of + plural noun:</strong> the main verb agrees with “one”. “One of my friends has arrived.”</li><li><strong>A number of + plural noun:</strong> plural verb. “A number of students are absent.”</li><li><strong>The number of + plural noun:</strong> singular verb. “The number of students is increasing.”</li><li><strong>Either…or / neither…nor:</strong> in standard exam patterns with mixed number, the verb agrees with the nearer subject. “Neither the teacher nor the students are late.”</li></ul><h2>Common error</h2><div class="example">Incorrect: Each of the books <s>are</s> useful.<br>Correct: Each of the books <strong>is</strong> useful.</div><h2>Remember</h2><p lang="kn">ಮುಖ್ಯ ಕರ್ತೃವನ್ನು ಗುರುತಿಸಿ; ಮಧ್ಯೆ ಬರುವ ಪದಗಳಿಂದ ಗೊಂದಲಗೊಳ್ಳಬೇಡಿ.</p>`},
{id:'active-passive',title:'Active & Passive Voice',category:'Grammar',minutes:6,description:'Understand the movement of subject and object, with tense and pronoun reminders.',letter:'↔',body:`<h2>The central pattern</h2><p>For a straightforward active clause with a direct object, the object can become the subject of the passive clause. Use the appropriate form of <strong>be + past participle (V3)</strong>.</p><div class="example">Active: Ravi writes a letter.<br>Passive: A letter <strong>is written</strong> by Ravi.</div><h2>Keep the tense</h2><ul><li>Simple present: writes → <strong>is / am / are written</strong></li><li>Simple past: wrote → <strong>was / were written</strong></li><li>Present continuous: is writing → <strong>is being written</strong></li><li>Present perfect: has written → <strong>has been written</strong></li><li>Simple future: will write → <strong>will be written</strong></li><li>Modal: can write → <strong>can be written</strong></li></ul><h2>Watch the pronouns</h2><div class="example">She helps him.<br><strong>He</strong> is helped by <strong>her</strong>.</div><h2>Common errors and limits</h2><p><strong>V3 is mandatory</strong> in the standard passive construction. “A letter is wrote” is incorrect; use “written”. The form of “be” must also agree with the new subject.</p><p>Intransitive verbs such as “arrive” have no direct object and do not form an ordinary object-based passive. “He arrived” has no standard passive transformation.</p><p>The “by” phrase is optional when the agent is unknown, unimportant or obvious: “The window was broken.”</p><h2>Exam trap</h2><p>Do not change the tense while transforming the sentence. “Ravi wrote a letter” becomes “A letter <strong>was written</strong> by Ravi”, not “is written”.</p><div class="example" lang="kn">ಕಾಲ ಬದಲಾಗಬಾರದು. ಮುಖ್ಯ ಕ್ರಿಯಾಪದದ V3 ರೂಪ ಬೇಕು.</div>`},
{id:'elt-methods',title:'ELT Approaches & Methods',category:'Pedagogy',minutes:6,description:'A clear comparison of language-teaching methods and their classroom signals.',letter:'ELT',body:`<h2>Approach, method and technique</h2><p>An <strong>approach</strong> reflects beliefs about language and learning. A <strong>method</strong> is an organised teaching plan informed by those beliefs. A <strong>technique</strong> is a specific classroom procedure.</p><h2>Recognise the classroom</h2><ul><li><strong>Grammar-Translation Method:</strong> explicit grammar rules, translation and emphasis on reading and writing.</li><li><strong>Direct Method:</strong> target-language use, oral interaction and meaning through demonstration or context.</li><li><strong>Audio-lingual Method:</strong> dialogue memorisation, imitation, repetition and pattern drills.</li><li><strong>Communicative Language Teaching:</strong> meaningful communication and communicative competence; language is used to complete purposes.</li><li><strong>Total Physical Response:</strong> learners respond physically to spoken commands, especially in early stages.</li></ul><h2>Example → identify the method</h2><div class="example">Teacher: “Stand up. Open the door.” Learners carry out the actions.<br><strong>Total Physical Response</strong>.</div><div class="example">Learners have different train timetables and ask one another questions to plan a journey.<br><strong>Communicative task</strong>: an information gap creates a reason to communicate.</div><h2>Common exam trap</h2><p>Communicative teaching values appropriate accuracy as well as fluency. It does <strong>not</strong> mean that grammar is never taught. A drill by itself is also not evidence of meaningful communication.</p><h2>Revision cue</h2><p>Translation → Grammar-Translation.<br>Repetition and patterns → Audio-lingual.<br>Meaning and purpose → Communicative.<br>Commands and actions → TPR.</p><p lang="kn">ತರಗತಿಯ ಚಟುವಟಿಕೆಯನ್ನು ಗಮನಿಸಿ; ವಿಧಾನವನ್ನು ಗುರುತಿಸಿ.</p>`}
];
const TESTS=[MOCK_TEST_7,{id:'grammar',title:'English Grammar Check',category:'Grammar',description:'Agreement, articles, voice and question tags. Find the rules that need a second look.',questions:[
{q:'Choose the correct verb: Each of the students ___ a notebook.',o:['have','has','are having','were having'],a:1,why:'“Each” is singular, so the simple-present verb is “has”. “Of the students” does not change the number of the subject.',note:'subject-verb-agreement'},
{q:'Choose the correct passive form: “Ravi wrote a letter.”',o:['A letter is written by Ravi.','A letter has written by Ravi.','A letter was written by Ravi.','A letter was wrote by Ravi.'],a:2,why:'The active is in the simple past. Use was/were + V3: “A letter was written by Ravi.”',note:'active-passive'},
{q:'Choose the correct article: She is ___ honest teacher.',o:['an','a','the','no article'],a:0,why:'“Honest” begins with a vowel sound because h is silent. The indefinite article is “an”.',note:null},
{q:'Choose the correct question tag: You are ready, ___?',o:['are you','isn’t it','don’t you','aren’t you'],a:3,why:'An affirmative statement normally takes a negative tag. Repeat the auxiliary “are” and the subject “you”: “aren’t you?”',note:null},
{q:'Choose the correct sentence.',o:['The number of applicants are increasing.','The number of applicants is increasing.','The number of applicants have increased yesterday.','The number of applicants were increases.'],a:1,why:'“The number of” has the singular head noun “number”, so the verb is “is”.',note:'subject-verb-agreement'}]},
{id:'pedagogy',title:'ELT Methods Check',category:'Pedagogy',description:'Read a classroom situation and identify the teaching method or principle.',questions:[
{q:'Learners physically carry out spoken commands. Which method is most clearly illustrated?',o:['Grammar-Translation','Audio-lingual Method','Direct Method','Total Physical Response'],a:3,why:'Total Physical Response connects spoken language with physical action.',note:'elt-methods'},
{q:'Which activity best creates a communicative information gap?',o:['Copying a paragraph from the board','Repeating one sentence in chorus','Exchanging different timetables to plan a journey','Memorising a list of verb forms'],a:2,why:'Each learner has information the other needs. Exchanging it serves a meaningful purpose.',note:'elt-methods'},
{q:'Dialogue memorisation and repeated pattern drills are especially associated with which method?',o:['Audio-lingual Method','Communicative Language Teaching','Grammar-Translation Method','Total Physical Response'],a:0,why:'The Audio-lingual Method emphasises imitation, memorisation and structural pattern practice.',note:'elt-methods'},
{q:'Which statement about Communicative Language Teaching is accurate?',o:['It forbids all grammar teaching.','It develops language use for meaningful purposes.','It requires translation in every lesson.','It treats silent copying as conversation.'],a:1,why:'CLT emphasises communicative competence and purposeful language use; it does not exclude grammar or accuracy.',note:'elt-methods'},
{q:'Explicit grammar rules and translation between the first language and target language are central to which method?',o:['Direct Method','Total Physical Response','Grammar-Translation Method','Task-based Language Teaching'],a:2,why:'Grammar-Translation uses explicit rules and translation, traditionally with emphasis on reading and writing.',note:'elt-methods'}]}];
const boot=window.__PORTAL_BOOT__||{};
const STORE=boot.storageKey||'inspired-guest-v2';
let storageOK=true,state;const defaults=()=>({profile:null,read:[],saved:[],watched:[],attempts:[],drafts:{},activity:{},goal:5,customNotes:[]});
let cloud={user:boot.user||null,version:boot.remote?.version||boot.cache?.version||0,base:boot.remote?.payload||boot.cache?.base||defaults(),pending:!!boot.cache?.pending,loaded:!!boot.remote,error:!!boot.user&&!boot.remote,saving:false,timer:null};
try{
 if(boot.user){state=Object.assign(defaults(),boot.remote?.payload||boot.cache?.payload||{});if(boot.cache?.pending&&boot.remote)state=mergeCloud(boot.cache.base,boot.cache.payload,boot.remote.payload);if(boot.legacy&&isAdmin()){state=mergeCloud(defaults(),boot.legacy,state);cloud.pending=true;}if(boot.guest){state=mergeCloud(defaults(),boot.guest,state);cloud.pending=true;}cloud.pending=cloud.pending||!same(state,cloud.base);}
 else state=Object.assign(defaults(),JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(STORE)||'null')||{});
}catch(e){state=defaults();storageOK=false;}
let currentFilter='All',listQuery='',savedOnly=false,quizIndex=0,reviewAttempt=null,toastTimer;
const allNotes=()=>[...NOTES,...state.customNotes];
const $=s=>document.querySelector(s);
function save(){if(cloud.user){cloud.pending=true;persistAccount();queueCloudSave();}else{try{localStorage.setItem(STORE,JSON.stringify(state));}catch(e){storageOK=false;toast('Storage is unavailable. Changes will last for this visit only.');}}}

function dayKey(d=new Date()){return new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-CA',{timeZone:'Asia/Kolkata',year:'numeric',month:'2-digit',day:'2-digit'}).format(d);}
function activity(){let k=dayKey();state.activity[k]=(state.activity[k]||0)+1;save();}
function toast(t){$('#toast').textContent=t;$('#toast').classList.add('show');clearTimeout(toastTimer);toastTimer=setTimeout(()=>$('#toast').classList.remove('show'),3200);}
function hydrateIcons(){document.querySelectorAll('[data-icon]').forEach(el=>el.innerHTML=icon(el.dataset.icon));}
function go(route){location.hash='#/'+route;}
function link(route,label,cls='button',i='arrow'){return `<a href="#/${route}" class="${cls}">${label}${icon(i)}</a>`;}
function external(url,label,cls='button',i='external'){return `<a href="${esc(url)}" class="${cls}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">${label}${icon(i)}</a>`;}
function intro(title,desc,label='YOUR LEARNING SPACE',right=''){return `<div class="page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">${esc(label)}</div><div class="intro-line"><div><h1>${esc(title)}</h1><p>${esc(desc)}</p></div>${right}</div></div>`;}
function empty(title,desc,action='notes',label='Browse free notes'){return `<div class="empty">${icon('book')}<h3>${esc(title)}</h3><p>${esc(desc)}</p><a class="button" href="#/${action}" data-action="reset-filters">${esc(label)}${icon('arrow')}</a></div>`;}
function stats(){const acc=accuracy();return `<div class="stats"><div class="stat"><div class="iconbox">${icon('book')}</div><div><small>Notes completed</small><b>${state.read.length}<span>/ ${allNotes().length}</span></b></div></div><div class="stat"><div class="iconbox">${icon('test')}</div><div><small>Practice attempts</small><b>${state.attempts.length}<span>tests</span></b></div></div><div class="stat"><div class="iconbox">${icon('video')}</div><div><small>Classes completed</small><b>${state.watched.length}<span>videos</span></b></div></div><div class="stat"><div class="iconbox">${icon('target')}</div><div><small>Practice accuracy</small><b>${acc===null?'—':acc+'%'}<span>${acc===null?'start a test':''}</span></b></div></div></div>`;}
function accuracy(){let a=state.attempts.reduce((s,x)=>s+x.correct+x.wrong,0),c=state.attempts.reduce((s,x)=>s+x.correct,0);return a?Math.round(c/a*100):null;}
function weekDays(){let now=new Date(),t=new Date(now.toLocaleString('en-US',{timeZone:'Asia/Kolkata'}));let start=new Date(t.getFullYear(),t.getMonth(),t.getDate());start.setDate(start.getDate()-((start.getDay()+6)%7));return Array.from({length:7},(_,i)=>{let d=new Date(start);d.setDate(start.getDate()+i);let k=`${d.getFullYear()}-${String(d.getMonth()+1).padStart(2,'0')}-${String(d.getDate()).padStart(2,'0')}`;return {key:k,label:['M','T','W','T','F','S','S'][i],n:d.getDate(),count:state.activity[k]||0,today:k===dayKey()};});}
function weeklyPanel(){let ds=weekDays(),done=ds.filter(x=>x.count).length;return `<div class="panel"><div class="week-head"><h3>Your weekly rhythm</h3><span>${done} active ${done===1?'day':'days'}</span></div><div class="week">${ds.map(d=>`<div class="day">${d.label}<div class="day-circle ${d.count?'done':''} ${d.today?'today':''}" title="${d.count} learning activities">${d.count?'✓':d.n}</div></div>`).join('')}</div><div class="goal-label"><span>Weekly goal</span><span>${done} / ${state.goal} days</span></div><div class="small-progress"><span style="width:${Math.min(100,done/state.goal*100)}%"></span></div><p class="goal-foot">${done>=state.goal?'Goal reached. Keep the momentum!':'One small step each day adds up.'}</p></div>`;}
function heroArt(){return `<div class="hero-art" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 260 260" fill="none"><g transform="translate(28 40) rotate(-8 100 100)"><path d="M35 124 114 160l92-49-81-33-90 46Z" fill="#8b793d" stroke="#c4ac66"/><path d="m35 124 1 17 77 35 92-49 1-16-92 49-79-36Z" fill="#333a20" stroke="#a48e4b"/><path d="m50 102 78 34 86-45-77-31-87 42Z" fill="#c4ac66" stroke="#e6ce87"/><path d="m50 102 1 17 76 33 86-45 1-16-86 45-78-34Z" fill="#565435" stroke="#c4ac66"/><path d="m66 83 66 29 72-38-67-26-71 35Z" fill="#343e24" stroke="#ad995c"/><path d="m66 83 1 13 65 28 71-38 1-12-72 38-66-29Z" fill="#66613b" stroke="#ad995c"/><path d="m112 55 32-15 48 18-33 16-47-19Z" fill="#e6ca7c"/><path d="m90 188 81-139 8 5-79 140-14 11 4-17Z" fill="#cbb572" stroke="#e7ce8a"/><path d="m86 205 4-17 10 6-14 11Z" fill="#f3dd9b"/><path d="m86 205 4-7 3 2-7 5Z" fill="#20291b"/></g><path d="m206 31 3 9 9 3-9 3-3 9-3-9-9-3 9-3 3-9Z" fill="#d6bd72"/><circle cx="37" cy="76" r="3" fill="#a89557"/><path d="M42 187h10m-5-5v10M225 166h8m-4-4v8" stroke="#8d8048"/></svg></div>`;}
function home(){const name=state.profile?`, ${esc(state.profile.name.split(' ')[0])}`:'';const date=new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-IN',{day:'numeric',month:'short',year:'numeric',timeZone:'Asia/Kolkata'}).format(new Date());const unread=allNotes().filter(n=>!state.read.includes(n.id));return `<div class="greeting-row"><div><h1>A good day to learn${name}.</h1><p>ಸ್ನೇಹಿತರೆ, your next step starts right here.</p></div><div class="date-label">${icon('calendar')}${date}</div></div><section class="hero"><div class="hero-copy"><div class="eyebrow">${icon('spark')}LEARN • EXCEL • INSPIRE</div><h1>English Learning &amp;<br><em>Exam Preparation</em></h1><p>Free Video Lessons • Study Notes • PYQs • Mock Tests</p><div class="hero-actions">${link('videos','Watch Free Video Classes','button','play')}${link('tests','Take a Practice Test','button secondary','arrow')}</div></div>${heroArt()}</section>${stats()}<div class="dashboard-columns"><div><div class="section-head"><div><h2>Where would you like to begin?</h2><p class="section-sub">A clear path from understanding to confidence.</p></div></div><div class="pathway">${[['notes','notes','Free study notes','Read. Understand. Revise.'],['tests','test','Practice tests','Attempt. Review. Improve.'],['videos','video','Video classes','Watch. Pause. Learn.']].map(([r,i,t,d])=>`<a class="path-card" href="#/${r}"><div class="path-icon">${icon(i)}</div><span class="go">${icon('arrow')}</span><h3>${t}</h3><p>${d}</p></a>`).join('')}</div><div class="section-head"><div><h2>${state.read.length?'Your next chapter':'Start with a quick read'}</h2><p class="section-sub">${unread.length?'Small notes. Strong foundations.':'Revisit a topic and strengthen your understanding.'}</p></div>${link('notes','All notes','text-link')}</div><div class="panel">${(unread.length?unread:allNotes()).slice(0,3).map(n=>`<div class="note-row"><div class="note-symbol">${icon('notes')}</div><div><h3>${esc(n.title)}</h3><p>${esc(n.category)} <span>•</span> ${noteMeta(n)} <span>•</span> Free</p></div>${link('notes/'+n.id,'Read note','text-link')}</div>`).join('')}</div><div class="section-head" style="margin-top:24px"><div><h2>Learn → Practise → Grow</h2><p class="section-sub">Your effort becomes visible, one step at a time.</p></div>${link('progress','My progress','text-link')}</div></div><aside class="dashboard-aside">${weeklyPanel()}<div class="panel premium-mini">${icon('crown')}<h3>Ready for a<br>deeper learning journey?</h3><p>Explore premium courses, recorded lessons and study material in the InspirED app.</p>${link('premium','Explore the InspirED App')}<small>Premium learning through APPX • Android</small></div><p class="tip"><strong>✦ A note for your journey</strong>Revise the rule you missed. Every mistake can become one less mistake in the exam.</p></aside></div>`;}
function bookmarkButton(n){let b=state.saved.includes(n.id);return `<button class="icon-button ${b?'saved':''}" data-action="bookmark" data-id="${esc(n.id)}" aria-label="${b?'Remove saved note':'Save note'}: ${esc(n.title)}" aria-pressed="${b}">${icon('bookmark')}</button>`;}
function noteMeta(n){return n.readingLabel||`${n.minutes} min read`;}
function noteCard(n){return `<article class="resource-card"><a class="resource-art ${n.category.toLowerCase()}" href="#/notes/${n.id}" data-letter="${esc(n.letter||'N')}">${icon(n.category==='Literature'?'book':'notes')}<p>${esc(n.category.toUpperCase())} / QUICK REVISION</p></a><div class="card-body"><div class="tag free">${n.pdf?'ORIGINAL PDF · FREE':'SAMPLE STUDY NOTE · FREE'} ${state.read.includes(n.id)?' · COMPLETED':''}</div><h3>${esc(n.title)}</h3><p>${esc(n.description)}</p><div class="card-meta"><span>${noteMeta(n)}</span><span>${esc(n.languageLabel||'English + Kannada cues')}</span></div><div class="card-actions">${link('notes/'+n.id,'Read note','button secondary')}${bookmarkButton(n)}</div></div></article>`;}
function filters(categories,placeholder){return `<div class="filterbar"><div class="chips">${['All',...categories].map(c=>`<button class="chip ${currentFilter===c?'active':''}" data-action="filter" data-value="${esc(c)}" aria-pressed="${currentFilter===c}">${esc(c)}</button>`).join('')}${route().split('/')[0]==='notes'?`<button class="chip ${savedOnly?'active':''}" data-action="saved-only" aria-pressed="${savedOnly}">♡ Saved (${state.saved.length})</button>`:''}</div><label class="filter-search">${icon('search')}<input id="filter-search" aria-label="${esc(placeholder)}" placeholder="${esc(placeholder)}" value="${esc(listQuery)}"></label></div>`;}
function notesPage(){return intro('Free study notes','Build your understanding. Save what matters. Come back for a quick revision.','READ → UNDERSTAND → REVISE',`<span class="resource-count">${allNotes().length} free notes</span>`)+filters(['Vocabulary','Grammar','Literature','Pedagogy'],'Search notes…')+`<div class="notice">The original homophones PDF is available below. Other notes are labelled as samples. Printed exam references in supplied material have not been independently verified.</div><div id="resource-results">${noteResults()}</div>`;}
function noteResults(){let ns=allNotes().filter(n=>(currentFilter==='All'||n.category===currentFilter)&&(!savedOnly||state.saved.includes(n.id))&&(n.title+' '+n.description+' '+n.category+' '+(n.searchTerms||'')).toLowerCase().includes(listQuery.toLowerCase()));return ns.length?`<div class="resource-grid">${ns.map(noteCard).join('')}</div>`:empty('No notes found','Try a different topic or clear your filters.','notes','Show all notes');}

function homophoneCards(query=''){
 const term=query.trim().toLowerCase();
 const matches=HOMOPHONE_SETS.filter(s=>!term||s.words.some(w=>(w.word+' '+w.meaning).toLowerCase().includes(term))||String(s.number)===term);
 return `<p class="vocab-results-count" role="status" aria-live="polite">${matches.length} of ${HOMOPHONE_SETS.length} sets${term?' match your search':''}</p>`+(matches.length?`<div class="vocab-grid">${matches.map(s=>`<article class="vocab-card" id="vocab-set-${s.number}"><div class="vocab-set-label">SET ${String(s.number).padStart(3,'0')}</div><dl>${s.words.map(w=>`<div class="vocab-word"><dt>${esc(w.word)}</dt><dd>${esc(w.meaning)}</dd></div>`).join('')}</dl><details class="source-reference"><summary>Printed exam context · unverified</summary><p>${esc(s.printedReference)}</p></details></article>`).join('')}</div>`:`<div class="empty"><h3>No matching sets</h3><p>Try a word such as “stationary”, a meaning, or a set number from 1 to 100.</p><button class="button secondary" data-action="clear-vocab-search">Clear search</button></div>`);
}
function pdfNoteReader(n,done){
 return `<div class="reader pdf-note-reader">${link('notes','Back to notes','back','back')}<div class="reader-top"><span class="tag free">FREE · VOCABULARY · ORIGINAL PDF</span>${bookmarkButton(n)}</div><h1>${esc(n.title)}</h1><div class="reading-meta"><span>${esc(noteMeta(n))}</span><span>Original source wording retained</span>${done?'<span class="green">✓ Completed</span>':''}</div><div class="pdf-actions">${external(n.pdf,'Open original PDF','button secondary','external')}<a href="${esc(n.pdf)}" download="${esc(n.sourceFileName)}" class="button">${icon('download')}Download PDF</a></div><div class="notice source-quality"><strong>About this reference:</strong> The supplied list includes both homophones and commonly confused words; some entries do not have identical pronunciations. This reading view preserves the source wording. Its printed examination references are unverified and should not be treated as verified PYQs.</div><section aria-labelledby="vocab-reader-title"><div class="section-head"><div><h2 id="vocab-reader-title">Read the 100 sets</h2><p class="section-sub">Larger text for your phone. Search a word, meaning or set number.</p></div></div><label class="filter-search vocab-search">${icon('search')}<input id="vocab-search" type="search" aria-label="Search homophone sets" placeholder="Try principal, stationary, or a meaning…" autocomplete="off"></label><div id="vocab-results">${homophoneCards()}</div></section><details class="original-pdf-preview"><summary>View the original two-page PDF</summary><iframe class="pdf-frame" src="${esc(n.pdf)}" title="Original PDF: ${esc(n.title)}" loading="lazy"></iframe><p class="small muted">If the PDF does not display on your phone, use “Open original PDF” or “Download PDF” above.</p></details><div class="reader-bottom"><p>${done?'Completed — revisit the words whenever you need to.':'When you have finished reading, mark this note complete.'}</p><button class="button" data-action="complete-note" data-id="${n.id}" ${done?'disabled':''}>${icon('check')}${done?'Completed':'Mark as complete'}</button></div><div class="hero-actions">${link('progress','See my progress','button secondary','chart')}${link('notes','Browse more notes','button secondary','book')}</div></div>`;
}

function reader(id){let n=allNotes().find(x=>x.id===id);if(!n)return notFound();const done=state.read.includes(id);if(n.pdf)return pdfNoteReader(n,done);return `<div class="reader">${link('notes','Back to notes','back','back')}<div class="reader-top"><span class="tag free">FREE · ${esc(n.category.toUpperCase())}</span>${bookmarkButton(n)}</div><h1>${esc(n.title)}</h1><div class="reading-meta"><span>${noteMeta(n)}</span><span>Prototype study note</span>${done?'<span class="green">✓ Completed</span>':''}</div><article class="reading-body">${n.body}</article><div class="reader-bottom"><p>${done?'Completed — you can return to this note any time.':'Read the note, then mark it complete to track your progress.'}</p><button class="button" data-action="complete-note" data-id="${id}" ${done?'disabled':''}>${icon('check')}${done?'Completed':'Mark as complete'}</button></div><div class="hero-actions">${id.startsWith('preview-note-')?`<button class="button secondary" data-action="download-note" data-id="${id}">${icon('download')}Download text note</button>`:`<a class="button secondary" href="assets/notes/${id}.txt" download="InspirED-${id}.txt">${icon('download')}Download text note</a>`}${link('tests','Practise now','button secondary')}</div></div>`;}

function questionPassage(q){return q.passage?`<section class="reading-passage" aria-label="Source reading passage"><h3>${esc(q.passageLead)}</h3><p>${esc(q.passage)}</p><small>Answer according to this supplied practice passage.</small></section>`:'';}
function sectionReview(t,a){const groups=[...new Set(t.questions.map(q=>q.section))];return `<section class="panel section-review"><h2>Section-wise review</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table class="history-table"><thead><tr><th>SECTION</th><th>CORRECT</th><th>WRONG</th><th>SKIPPED</th><th>SCORE</th></tr></thead><tbody>${groups.map(section=>{let c=0,w=0,k=0;t.questions.forEach((q,i)=>{if(q.section!==section)return;if(a.answers[i]===null)k++;else if(a.answers[i]===q.a)c++;else w++;});return `<tr><td>${esc(section)}</td><td>${c}</td><td>${w}</td><td>${k}</td><td>${c-w*.25} / ${c+w+k}</td></tr>`;}).join('')}</tbody></table></div></section>`;}
function originalSourceDetails(q){const original=MOCK_TEST_7_SOURCE.find(x=>x.number===q.number);return original.o.map((o,i)=>`<div class="answer-option">${'ABCD'[i]}. ${esc(o)}</div>`).join('')+`<p><strong>Original supplied key:</strong> ${'ABCD'[original.sourceAnswer]}</p><p><strong>Original supplied explanation:</strong> ${esc(original.sourceSolution)}</p>`;}
function mock7ReviewPage(){const dist=MOCK_TEST_7_SOURCE.reduce((n,q)=>(n[q.a]++,n),[0,0,0,0]);return `${link('admin','Back to Admin review','back','back')}${intro('Mock Test 7 — source & adaptation review','100 scored questions. Compare the 14 adapted items with the exact original wording, options, keys and explanations.','ADMIN · SOURCE REVIEW')}<div class="notice">Original practice and adapted model questions, not verified PYQs. The source DOCX is unchanged. All 100 question numbers and source key positions are retained.</div><section class="panel"><h2>Saved syllabus basis</h2><p class="small muted" style="margin:12px 0">${esc(MOCK_TEST_7.syllabusReference)}</p><p class="small muted">${esc(MOCK_TEST_7.syllabusBasis)}</p><p class="small muted" style="margin-top:14px">Relevant checkpoints: parts of speech; preposition use; time and tense; finite and non-finite verbs; error correction; direct and reported speech; degrees of comparison; active and passive voice; one-word substitution.</p></section><section class="panel" style="margin-top:20px"><h2>Source answer distribution</h2><p class="small muted" style="margin:12px 0">A: ${dist[0]} · B: ${dist[1]} · C: ${dist[2]} · D: ${dist[3]}. Option positions are retained, so this practice is not balanced by answer position.</p>${link('test/mock-test-7','Open the 100-question practice test','button secondary')}</section><div class="section-head" style="margin-top:25px"><h2>14 adapted source items</h2></div>${MOCK_TEST_7.reviewItems.map(q=>`<article class="answer-card editorial-review-item"><span class="tag sample">QUESTION ${q.number} · ADAPTED MODEL · SCORED</span><p class="small gold">Syllabus topic: ${esc(q.syllabusTopic)}</p><p class="editorial-note"><strong>What changed:</strong> ${esc(q.changeSummary)}</p><h3>${esc(q.q)}</h3>${q.o.map((o,i)=>`<div class="answer-option ${i===q.a?'correct':''}">${'ABCD'[i]}. ${esc(o)}${i===q.a?' ✓':''}</div>`).join('')}<p><strong>Revised key:</strong> ${'ABCD'[q.a]}</p><p><strong>Revised explanation:</strong> ${esc(q.why)}</p><details class="source-wording"><summary>Compare original question, options and source key</summary><p class="editorial-note"><strong>Original issue:</strong> ${esc(q.reviewReason)}</p><p class="source-verbatim">${esc(q.sourceQuestion)}</p>${originalSourceDetails(q)}</details>${q.references?.length?`<div class="editorial-references">${q.references.map(r=>external(r.url,r.title,'text-link')).join('<br>')}</div>`:''}</article>`).join('')}`;}

function testCard(t){let attempts=state.attempts.filter(x=>x.testId===t.id),best=attempts.length?Math.max(...attempts.map(x=>x.score)):null,draft=state.drafts[t.id],imported=t.kind==='imported';return `<article class="resource-card ${imported?'imported-test-card':''}"><div class="card-body"><div class="tag sample">${imported?'SUPPLIED PRACTICE · FREE · NOT PYQs':'AI-GENERATED SAMPLE · FREE'}</div><h3>${esc(t.title)}</h3><p>${esc(t.description)}</p><div class="card-meta"><span>${t.questions.length} scored questions</span><span>Self-paced</span><span>+1 / −0.25</span></div>${imported?`<p class="test-import-meta">${t.sourceCount} source items · ${t.reviewItems.length} adapted to clarify the question<br>Maximum score: ${t.questions.length}. Original source numbers retained.</p>`:''}${best!==null?`<p class="green small">Best score: ${best} / ${t.questions.length}</p>`:''}<div class="card-actions"><button class="button secondary" data-action="start-test" data-id="${t.id}">${draft?'Resume practice':'Start practice'}${icon('arrow')}</button></div></div></article>`;}

function testsPage(){let last=state.attempts.at(-1);return intro('Practice with a purpose','Understand the rule. Attempt the question. Learn from every answer.','PRACTISE → REVIEW → IMPROVE')+`<div class="notice">Mock Test 7 uses the institute’s original practice paper. All ${MOCK_TEST_7.questions.length} questions are included; ${MOCK_TEST_7.reviewItems.length} have been revised using the institute’s saved syllabus topics and are labelled as adapted model practice. Other short tests are AI-generated samples. These are not verified PYQs. Scoring: +1 correct, −0.25 wrong, 0 skipped.</div>${last?`<div class="sticky-note">${icon('chart')}<span>Your latest score: <strong>${last.score} / ${last.total}</strong> in ${esc(last.title)}</span><button class="button small-btn secondary" data-action="review-attempt" data-id="${last.id}">Review answers ${icon('arrow')}</button></div>`:''}<div class="resource-grid">${TESTS.map(testCard).join('')}</div><div class="panel" style="margin-top:25px"><h3>A useful routine</h3><p class="muted small" style="margin-top:10px">Attempt without looking up the answer. Review the explanation. Revisit the concept. Retake when you are ready.</p></div>`;}

function startTest(id){const t=TESTS.find(x=>x.id===id);if(!t)return; if(!state.drafts[id]){state.drafts[id]={answers:Array(t.questions.length).fill(null),flags:[],startedAt:Date.now(),index:0,revision:t.revision||'sample-v1'};save();}quizIndex=state.drafts[id].index||0;const target='test/'+id;if(route()===target)render();else go(target);}
function quiz(id){let t=TESTS.find(x=>x.id===id);if(!t)return notFound();if(!state.drafts[id])return intro(t.title,'Original practice questions. Start when you are ready.')+testCard(t);let d=state.drafts[id];quizIndex=Math.min(d.index||0,t.questions.length-1);let q=t.questions[quizIndex],answered=d.answers.filter(x=>x!==null).length,flag=d.flags.includes(quizIndex),imported=t.kind==='imported';return `${link('tests','Save & return to tests','back','back')}<div class="page-intro"><h1>${esc(t.title)}</h1><p>${imported?'Scored review edition · Original practice, not PYQs':'AI-generated model practice'} · ${cloud.user?'Progress is saved to your account while you practise online.':'Progress stays on this device. Sign in to save it across devices.'}</p></div>${imported?`<div class="notice test-scope">${t.questions.length} questions · Maximum: ${t.questions.length} marks. Includes ${t.reviewItems.length} adapted model items mapped to your saved syllabus topics. Original source numbers are retained.</div>`:''}<div class="quiz-layout ${imported?'source-quiz':''}"><section class="quiz-card"><div class="quiz-meta"><span>QUESTION ${quizIndex+1} OF ${t.questions.length}${q.number?' · SOURCE Q.'+q.number:''}</span><span>+1 correct · −0.25 wrong</span></div>${q.adapted?'<span class="tag sample adapted-label">ADAPTED MODEL PRACTICE</span>':''}<div class="small-progress"><span style="width:${answered/t.questions.length*100}%"></span></div>${questionPassage(q)}<h2 class="quiz-question">${esc(q.q)}</h2><div class="options" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Answer options">${q.o.map((o,i)=>`<button class="option" role="radio" aria-checked="${d.answers[quizIndex]===i}" data-action="answer" data-id="${id}" data-value="${i}"><span class="letter">${'ABCD'[i]}</span><span>${esc(o)}</span></button>`).join('')}</div><div class="quiz-footer"><button class="button secondary" data-action="previous" data-id="${id}" ${quizIndex===0?'disabled':''}>${icon('back')}Previous</button><button class="button ghost" data-action="flag" data-id="${id}" aria-label="${flag?'Unflag question':'Flag for review'}" aria-pressed="${flag}">${icon('flag')}<span class="flag-label">${flag?'Unflag question':'Flag for review'}</span></button><button class="button" data-action="next" data-id="${id}" ${quizIndex===t.questions.length-1?'disabled':''}>Next${icon('arrow')}</button></div>${d.answers[quizIndex]!==null?`<button class="text-link" data-action="clear-answer" data-id="${id}" style="margin-top:15px">Clear answer</button>`:''}</section><aside class="panel quiz-aside"><h3>Question navigator</h3><div class="question-grid">${t.questions.map((n,i)=>`<button class="q-number ${i===quizIndex?'current':''} ${d.answers[i]!==null?'answered':''} ${d.flags.includes(i)?'flagged':''}" data-action="jump" data-id="${id}" data-value="${i}" aria-label="${n.number?'Source question '+n.number:'Question '+(i+1)}${d.answers[i]!==null?', answered':''}${d.flags.includes(i)?', flagged':''}" ${i===quizIndex?'aria-current="step"':''}>${n.number||i+1}</button>`).join('')}</div><div class="legend"><span><i></i>Answered</span><span><i class="flag"></i>Flagged</span></div><p><strong>${answered} answered</strong> · ${t.questions.length-answered} skipped<br>${d.flags.length} flagged for review</p><button class="button" data-action="submit-dialog" data-id="${id}">Finish & review ${icon('check')}</button><p class="goal-foot">Take your time. This practice has no time limit.</p></aside></div>`;}

function confirmSubmit(id){const t=TESTS.find(x=>x.id===id),d=state.drafts[id],skipped=d.answers.filter(x=>x===null).length;showModal(`<h2>Ready to review?</h2><p>${t.questions.length-skipped} answered · ${skipped} skipped · ${d.flags.length} flagged.<br>Skipped questions score 0. You can retake this practice after reviewing the explanations.</p><div class="dialog-actions"><button class="button secondary" data-action="close-modal">Keep practising</button><button class="button" data-action="submit-test" data-id="${id}">Submit practice ${icon('check')}</button></div>`);}
function submitTest(id){let t=TESTS.find(x=>x.id===id),d=state.drafts[id];if(!d)return;let correct=0,wrong=0;d.answers.forEach((x,i)=>{if(x===null)return;x===t.questions[i].a?correct++:wrong++;});let a={id:'a'+Date.now()+'-'+Math.random().toString(36).slice(2,9),testId:id,title:t.title,testRevision:t.revision||'sample-v1',questionNumbers:t.questions.map((q,i)=>q.number||i+1),total:t.questions.length,answers:d.answers,correct,wrong,skipped:t.questions.length-correct-wrong,score:correct-wrong*.25,finishedAt:Date.now()};state.attempts.push(a);delete state.drafts[id];activity();$('#modal').close();reviewAttempt=a;go('result/'+a.id);}
function resultPage(id){let a=state.attempts.find(x=>x.id===id),t=a&&TESTS.find(x=>x.id===a.testId);if(!a||!t)return notFound();let weak=[...new Set(t.questions.filter((q,i)=>a.answers[i]!==q.a).map(q=>q.note).filter(Boolean))],imported=t.kind==='imported';return `${link('tests','Back to practice tests','back','back')}<div class="result-banner"><div><div class="eyebrow">EVERY ATTEMPT IS A STEP FORWARD</div><h1>Your practice, reviewed.</h1><p class="muted small" style="margin-top:9px">${esc(a.title)} · ${imported?'Supplied original practice — scored review edition':'AI-generated model questions'}</p><div class="result-metrics"><div><b>${a.correct}</b>Correct</div><div><b>${a.wrong}</b>Incorrect</div><div><b>${a.skipped}</b>Skipped</div></div></div><div><div class="result-score">${a.score}<small> / ${a.total}</small></div><p class="small muted">+1 correct · −0.25 wrong</p></div></div>${imported?`<div class="notice">All ${t.questions.length} questions count in this attempt, including ${t.reviewItems.length} adapted model items. Their explanations describe the clarified rule; the original versions are retained for comparison.</div>`:''}<div class="hero-actions" style="margin:0 0 25px">${link('progress','See my progress')}<button class="button secondary" data-action="start-test" data-id="${t.id}">Retake practice ${icon('arrow')}</button></div>${weak.length?`<div class="panel" style="margin-bottom:25px"><h3>Your next useful step</h3><p class="small muted" style="margin:9px 0">Revisit these notes before your next attempt.</p>${weak.map(n=>link('notes/'+n,allNotes().find(x=>x.id===n)?.title||'Review note','text-link')).join('<br>')}</div>`:''}${imported?sectionReview(t,a):''}<h2>Answers & explanations</h2>${t.questions.map((q,i)=>`<article class="answer-card"><span class="tag ${a.answers[i]===q.a?'free':'sample'}">${q.number?'SOURCE Q.'+q.number:'QUESTION '+(i+1)} · ${a.answers[i]===null?'SKIPPED':a.answers[i]===q.a?'CORRECT':'INCORRECT'}</span>${q.passage?`<details class="review-passage"><summary>Read the source passage</summary>${questionPassage(q)}</details>`:''}${q.adapted?'<p class="small gold">Adapted model practice · '+esc(q.syllabusTopic)+'</p>':''}<h3>${esc(q.q)}</h3>${q.o.map((o,j)=>`<div class="answer-option ${j===q.a?'correct':a.answers[i]===j?'incorrect':''}">${'ABCD'[j]}. ${esc(o)} ${j===q.a?'✓ Correct answer':''}${a.answers[i]===j?' · Your answer':''}</div>`).join('')}<p><strong>${q.adapted?'Revised explanation':imported?'Source explanation':'Why'}:</strong> ${esc(q.why)}</p>${q.teacherNote?`<p class="editorial-note"><strong>Editorial clarification:</strong> ${esc(q.teacherNote)}</p>`:''}${q.sourceQuestion?`<details class="source-wording"><summary>Original source wording and labels</summary><p class="source-verbatim">${esc(q.sourceQuestion)}</p>${q.adapted?originalSourceDetails(q):''}</details>`:''}</article>`).join('')}`;}

function videoCard(v){return `<article class="resource-card video-card"><a class="video-thumb" href="#/videos/${v.id}" aria-label="Watch ${esc(v.title)}"><img src="https://img.youtube.com/vi/${v.id}/hqdefault.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"><span class="play">${icon('play')}</span><span class="duration">${v.duration}</span></a><div class="card-body"><span class="tag free">${esc(v.category.toUpperCase())} · ${state.watched.includes(v.id)?'COMPLETED':'FREE VIDEO'}</span><h3>${esc(v.title)}</h3><div class="card-actions">${link('videos/'+v.id,'Watch class','button secondary','play')}</div></div></article>`;}
function videosPage(){return intro('Free video classes','Learn at your own pace. Pause, revisit and make every concept your own.','WATCH → UNDERSTAND → APPLY',`<span class="resource-count">${VIDEOS.length} catalogue entries</span>`)+filters(['Grammar','Literature','Pedagogy','Vocabulary','Phonology','PYQs','General'],'Search video classes…')+`<div id="resource-results">${videoResults()}</div><p class="progress-note">Catalogue and original titles carried over from inspiredinstitute.in. Titles containing “PYQs” are the original video labels; individual question references have not been audited in this prototype.</p>`;}
function videoResults(){let vs=VIDEOS.filter(v=>(currentFilter==='All'||v.category===currentFilter)&&(v.title+' '+v.category).toLowerCase().includes(listQuery.toLowerCase()));return vs.length?`<div class="resource-grid">${vs.map(videoCard).join('')}</div>`:empty('No classes found','Try another topic or clear your search.','videos','Show all classes');}
function videoDetail(id){let v=VIDEOS.find(x=>x.id===id);if(!v)return notFound();let done=state.watched.includes(id);return `<div class="video-detail">${link('videos','Back to video classes','back','back')}<div id="player"><div class="video-privacy">${icon('video')}<h2>Make space for a good lesson.</h2><p>Play the class here using YouTube, or open it directly on YouTube. Your completion is updated when you mark the class complete.</p><button class="button" data-action="load-video" data-id="${id}">${icon('play')}Play video class</button></div></div><p class="player-fallback">Video not playing? ${external('https://www.youtube.com/watch?v='+id,'Watch on YouTube','text-link')}</p><h1>${esc(v.title)}</h1><div class="reading-meta"><span>${esc(v.category)}</span><span>${v.duration}</span><span>Free class</span></div><div class="video-actions"><button class="button" data-action="complete-video" data-id="${id}" ${done?'disabled':''}>${icon('check')}${done?'Completed':'Mark class complete'}</button>${link('notes','Explore study notes','button secondary','book')}</div><div class="notice info">Pause when you need to. Write one key rule. Try one question. That is progress.</div></div>`;}
function progressPage(){let ds=weekDays(),max=Math.max(3,...ds.map(x=>x.count));return intro('Your effort, made visible.','Your learning journey starts here. Access courses, tests and progress tracking.','MY PROGRESS')+progressNotice()+stats()+`<div class="progress-grid"><section class="panel"><div class="section-head"><h3>Your learning activity</h3><label class="small muted">Weekly goal <select id="goal" aria-label="Weekly learning goal">${[3,4,5,6,7].map(n=>`<option value="${n}" ${state.goal===n?'selected':''}>${n} days</option>`).join('')}</select></label></div><div class="chart-bars">${ds.map(d=>`<div class="activity-bar ${d.today?'today':''}" title="${d.count} completed learning activities"><span>${d.count}</span><i style="height:${Math.max(3,d.count/max*100)}px"></i><span>${d.label}</span></div>`).join('')}</div><p class="progress-note">A completed note, class or test adds one activity.</p></section><section class="panel"><h3>Your reading path</h3>${allNotes().map(n=>`<a class="progress-row" href="#/notes/${n.id}"><span>${esc(n.title)}<small>${esc(n.category)}</small></span><span class="${state.read.includes(n.id)?'green':'muted'} small">${state.read.includes(n.id)?'✓ Done':'Read →'}</span></a>`).join('')}</section></div><div class="section-head" style="margin-top:30px"><h2>Practice history</h2>${link('tests','Take a practice test','text-link')}</div>${state.attempts.length?`<div class="panel table-wrap"><table class="history-table"><thead><tr><th>TEST</th><th>DATE</th><th>SCORE</th><th>CORRECT</th><th>REVIEW</th></tr></thead><tbody>${state.attempts.slice().reverse().map(a=>`<tr><td>${esc(a.title)}</td><td>${new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-IN',{day:'numeric',month:'short',timeZone:'Asia/Kolkata'}).format(a.finishedAt)}</td><td class="gold">${a.score} / ${a.total}</td><td>${a.correct} / ${a.total}</td><td>${link('result/'+a.id,'Review','text-link')}</td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table></div>`:empty('Your first attempt starts the story.','Take a short practice test to see your score and explanations here.','tests','Start a practice test')}<div class="section-head" style="margin-top:28px"><h2>Saved for later</h2>${link('notes','Browse notes','text-link')}</div>${state.saved.length?`<div class="panel">${allNotes().filter(n=>state.saved.includes(n.id)).map(n=>`<a class="progress-row" href="#/notes/${n.id}"><span>${esc(n.title)}<small>${esc(n.category)} · ${noteMeta(n)}</small></span>${icon('arrow')}</a>`).join('')}</div>`:'<p class="muted small">Use the bookmark on any note to keep it close.</p>'}`;}
function premiumPage(){return `<div class="page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">YOUR NEXT CHAPTER</div></div><section class="premium-hero"><div><div class="eyebrow gold">${icon('crown')}PREMIUM LEARNING · IN THE APP</div><h1>One learning journey.<br>A little more <span class="gold">possibility.</span></h1><p>Build your foundation with free resources here. Continue your premium courses and study material through the existing InspirED Institute Android app.</p><div class="hero-actions">${external(APPX,'Get the InspirED Android App','button','phone')}${link('notes','Keep exploring free notes','button secondary')}</div><p class="small muted" style="margin-top:14px;font-size:10px">Opens the verified InspirED Institute listing on Google Play.</p></div><div class="phone" aria-hidden="true"><img src="assets/logo.jpeg" alt=""><h4>InspirED Institute</h4><p>Learn. Practise. Succeed.</p><div class="phone-course">HSTR & GPSTR<span>Premium learning</span></div><div class="phone-course">Your course material<span>Continue in the app →</span></div></div></section><div class="split-columns"><section class="panel"><h2>Start freely on the website</h2><ul class="checklist">${['Read and save free study notes','Attempt free model practice tests','Watch free video classes','Review your practice and learning progress'].map(s=>`<li>${icon('check')}<span>${s}</span></li>`).join('')}</ul></section><section class="panel"><h2>Continue premium learning in APPX</h2><ol class="steps"><li>Open the InspirED Institute app listing on Google Play.</li><li>Install or open the Android app.</li><li>Sign in with the mobile number used for your course.</li><li>Find your enrolled course and continue learning.</li></ol><p class="progress-note">Course access, enrolment and purchases are handled inside APPX. The website does not activate a paid course.</p></section></div><section class="faqs"><h2>A few useful answers</h2><details><summary>Do I need the app to use the free website resources?</summary><p>No. The free notes, model practice tests and video routes in this portal work here. The app is the route for premium course content.</p></details><details><summary>I have already enrolled. Should I pay again?</summary><p>Use the mobile number linked to your existing enrolment in the app. If your course is missing, contact the institute before purchasing again.</p></details><details><summary>Does my website progress appear in the app?</summary><p>Website progress is saved to your signed-in portal account. APPX enrolment and progress remain separate.</p></details><details><summary>What if I do not have an Android phone?</summary><p>The linked APPX app is for Android. You can continue using the free website resources in your browser. Contact the institute for help with premium access options.</p></details></section>`;}
function accountPage(){if(!cloud.user)return signedOutAccountPage();let p=state.profile;return intro('Student Portal','Your learning journey starts here. Access courses, tests and progress tracking.','YOUR PERSONAL LEARNING SPACE')+`<section class="panel account-card"><div class="account-tabs"><span class="chip active">Create Student Account</span><span class="chip">Student</span></div><h2>${p?'Your student profile':'Make this space yours.'}</h2><div class="account-identity"><span class="tag free">${esc(cloud.user?.role||'Student')}</span><p class="small">${cloud.user?'Signed in with ChatGPT · '+esc(cloud.user.email):'Sign in to connect your account.'}</p></div><p>Your display name, exam preference and progress are saved to your signed-in account.</p><form id="profile-form"><label class="form-field">Your display name<input name="name" required maxlength="45" placeholder="e.g. Ananya" value="${esc(p?.name||'')}"><small>A first name or nickname is enough.</small></label><label class="form-field">I am preparing for<select name="exam"><option value="HSTR & GPSTR">HSTR & GPSTR</option><option value="HSTR" ${p?.exam==='HSTR'?'selected':''}>HSTR</option><option value="GPSTR" ${p?.exam==='GPSTR'?'selected':''}>GPSTR</option><option value="Other competitive exams" ${p?.exam==='Other competitive exams'?'selected':''}>Other competitive exams</option></select></label><p class="form-error" id="profile-error" aria-live="polite"></p><button class="button" type="submit">${p?'Save profile':'Create My Account'}${icon('arrow')}</button></form>${cloud.user?`<div class="hero-actions">${link('progress','See my progress','text-link')}<a class="text-link" href="/signout-with-chatgpt?return_to=%2F" target="_top">Sign out of account</a></div>`:''}<div class="notice info" style="margin:23px 0 0">Portal roles: <strong>Student</strong> and <strong>Admin</strong>. Student accounts cannot assign themselves Admin access.</div></section>`;}
function adminPage(){return contentAdminPanel()+socialAdminPanel()+communityAdminPanel()+financeAdminPanel()+intro('Admin review workspace','Review the hybrid learning experience before a live-site integration.','ADMIN WORKSPACE')+`<div class="notice">Admin and Student are the only portal roles. Account progress is stored privately. Student data and learning insights require authenticated access, with Admin permissions checked on the server. Admin records and insights are restricted to your account.</div><section id="admin-learning" class="panel" style="margin-bottom:24px"><h2>Student learning insights</h2><p class="small muted">Loading saved learning…</p></section><div class="stats"><div class="stat"><div class="iconbox">${icon('notes')}</div><div><small>Free study notes</small><b>${allNotes().length}</b></div></div><div class="stat"><div class="iconbox">${icon('test')}</div><div><small>Model practice tests</small><b>${TESTS.length}</b></div></div><div class="stat"><div class="iconbox">${icon('video')}</div><div><small>Video catalogue entries</small><b>${VIDEOS.length}</b></div></div><div class="stat"><div class="iconbox">${icon('shield')}</div><div><small>Portal roles</small><b>2</b></div></div></div><section class="panel mock7-admin-summary" style="margin-bottom:22px"><h2>Mock Test 7 source review</h2><p class="small muted" style="margin:12px 0">${MOCK_TEST_7.sourceCount} source items · ${MOCK_TEST_7.questions.length} in the scored edition · ${MOCK_TEST_7.reviewItems.length} adapted. Compare the original items with the 14 syllabus-topic adaptations.</p>${link('review/mock-test-7','Review adapted questions','button secondary')}</section><div class="admin-layout"><section class="panel"><h2>Hybrid delivery</h2><div class="copy-row"><small>WEBSITE · FREE</small><p>Notes, practice tests, free video classes and account-based progress.</p></div><div class="copy-row"><small>APPX · PREMIUM</small><p>Existing Android app, enrolment and premium content.</p>${external(APPX,'Check app destination','text-link')}</div><div class="copy-row"><small>REVIEW SCOPE</small><p>Website resources are free. Premium courses continue through the existing APPX app.</p></div>${link('home','Open Student view','button secondary')}</section><section class="panel"><h2>Approved copy retained</h2>${[['SITE TITLE','InspirED Institute | Learn • Excel • Inspire'],['HOMEPAGE INTRO','Free Video Lessons • Study Notes • PYQs • Mock Tests'],['PRIMARY ACTION','Watch Free Video Classes'],['STUDENT PORTAL','Your learning journey starts here. Access courses, tests and progress tracking.'],['REGISTRATION','Create Student Account / Create My Account'],['TAGLINE','LEARN • EXCEL • INSPIRE']].map(([l,t])=>`<div class="copy-row"><small>${l}</small><p>${t}</p></div>`).join('')}</section></div><div class="section-head" style="margin-top:27px"><h2>Try adding a free study note</h2><span class="resource-count">Private Admin preview</span></div><section class="panel"><p class="small muted">Create a plain-text review note for your own account. It is available across your devices. Publishing notes to other student accounts is a later content-management step.</p><form id="admin-note-form"><div class="split-columns"><label class="form-field">Note title<input name="title" maxlength="80" required placeholder="Enter a clear topic title"></label><label class="form-field">Category<select name="category"><option>Grammar</option><option>Literature</option><option>Pedagogy</option><option>Vocabulary</option></select></label></div><label class="form-field">Note content<textarea name="body" required rows="5" maxlength="10000" style="font:inherit;color:inherit;padding:13px;background:#131b10;border:1px solid #444d35;border-radius:7px" placeholder="Add the concept, rule and a useful example…"></textarea></label><p id="admin-error" class="form-error" aria-live="polite"></p><button type="submit" class="button">Add preview note ${icon('arrow')}</button></form></section>`;}
function searchPage(q){let query=q.toLowerCase(),ns=allNotes().filter(n=>(n.title+' '+n.category+' '+n.description+' '+(n.searchTerms||'')).toLowerCase().includes(query)),vs=VIDEOS.filter(v=>(v.title+' '+v.category).toLowerCase().includes(query)),ts=TESTS.filter(t=>(t.title+' '+t.description).toLowerCase().includes(query));return intro('Find your next lesson',q?`Results for “${q}”`:'Search notes, model practice tests and free video classes.','SEARCH YOUR LEARNING SPACE')+`<form id="page-search" class="filter-search" style="max-width:600px;margin-bottom:25px">${icon('search')}<input name="q" aria-label="Search resources" placeholder="Try grammar, voice or pedagogy…" value="${esc(q)}"><button class="text-link" type="submit">Search</button></form>`+(q?(ns.length+vs.length+ts.length?`<p class="small muted">${ns.length+vs.length+ts.length} resources found</p>${ns.length?'<h2 class="search-label">STUDY NOTES</h2>':''}${ns.map(n=>hit('notes/'+n.id,n.category,n.title)).join('')}${ts.length?'<h2 class="search-label">PRACTICE TESTS</h2>':''}${ts.map(t=>hit('tests','Model practice',t.title)).join('')}${vs.length?'<h2 class="search-label">VIDEO CLASSES</h2>':''}${vs.map(v=>hit('videos/'+v.id,v.category,v.title)).join('')}`:empty('No matching resources yet','Try a shorter phrase or a broader topic.','notes','Browse free notes')):'');}
function hit(r,l,t){return `<a class="search-hit" href="#/${r}"><div><span class="tag">${esc(l)}</span><h3>${esc(t)}</h3></div>${icon('arrow')}</a>`;}
function notFound(){return intro('Let’s find your way back.','That learning resource is not in this prototype.')+empty('Choose your next step','Start from the overview or browse the free resources.','home','Back to overview');}
function showModal(html){$('#modal-content').innerHTML=html;$('#modal').showModal();}
function route(){return location.hash.replace(/^#\/?/,'')||'home';}
function renderMobileNavigation(base){
 const nav=document.getElementById('mobile-nav');if(!nav)return;
 const current=['test','result'].includes(base)?'tests':['account','progress','admin','review'].includes(base)?'account':base;
 nav.innerHTML=[['home','house','Home'],['videos','video','Classes'],['notes','notes','Notes'],['tests','test','Tests'],['account','user','Profile']].map(([path,symbol,label])=>`<a href="#/${path}" class="mobile-nav-item${current===path?' active':''}"${current===path?' aria-current="page"':''}>${icon(symbol)}<span>${label}</span></a>`).join('');
}
function render(keepScroll=false){const oldScroll=window.scrollY,[base,id,...rest]=route().split('/'),labels={home:'Overview',notes:'Free notes',tests:'Practice tests',test:'Practice test',result:'Practice review',videos:'Video classes',progress:'My progress',premium:'Premium courses',account:'Student Portal',admin:'Admin review',review:'Editorial review',search:'Search'};$('#crumb').textContent=labels[base]||'Overview';$('#nav').innerHTML=[['home','home','Overview'],['notes','notes','Free study notes'],['tests','test','Practice tests'],['videos','video','Video classes'],['progress','chart','My progress']].map(([r,i,t])=>`<a class="nav-link ${base===r||(r==='tests'&&['test','result'].includes(base))?'active':''}" href="#/${r}" ${base===r?'aria-current="page"':''}>${icon(i)}${t}${r==='notes'?`<span class="count">${allNotes().length}</span>`:''}</a>`).join('');$('.premium-link').classList.toggle('active',base==='premium');$('#profile-name').textContent=['admin','review'].includes(base)?'Admin review':state.profile?.name||'Student';$('#profile-sub').textContent=['admin','review'].includes(base)?'Protected Admin workspace':state.profile?.exam||'Your personal learning space';$('#avatar').textContent=['admin','review'].includes(base)?'A':state.profile?.name?.[0]?.toUpperCase()||'S';$('#main').innerHTML=base==='home'?home():base==='notes'?(id?reader(id):notesPage()):base==='tests'?testsPage():base==='test'?quiz(id):base==='result'?resultPage(id):base==='videos'?(id?videoDetail(id):videosPage()):base==='progress'?progressPage():base==='premium'?premiumPage():base==='account'?accountPage():base==='admin'?(isAdmin()?adminPage():accessRequired()):base==='review'&&id==='mock-test-7'?(isAdmin()?mock7ReviewPage():accessRequired()):base==='search'?searchPage(decodeURIComponent(id||'')):notFound();renderMobileNavigation(base);renderInstallCard(base);hydrateIcons();document.querySelector('.review-link').hidden=!isAdmin();updateCloudStatus();if(base==='admin'&&isAdmin()){loadAdminLearning();loadSocialAdmin();loadCommunityAdmin();loadContentAdmin();}if(base==='home'){$('#main').insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend','<section id="programme-discovery" class="panel programme-discovery" hidden></section>');loadProgrammeDiscovery();}$('#main').classList.remove('route-fade');void $('#main').offsetWidth;$('#main').classList.add('route-fade');if(!keepScroll){window.scrollTo(0,0);$('#main').focus({preventScroll:true});}else window.scrollTo(0,oldScroll);closeMenu();}
function closeMenu(){$('#sidebar').classList.remove('open');$('#shade').hidden=true;$('#menu').setAttribute('aria-expanded','false');}
$('#menu').addEventListener('click',()=>{let open=$('#sidebar').classList.toggle('open');$('#shade').hidden=!open;$('#menu').setAttribute('aria-expanded',String(open));});$('#shade').addEventListener('click',closeMenu);document.addEventListener('keydown',e=>{if(e.key==='Escape')closeMenu();});
window.addEventListener('hashchange',()=>{if(['notes','videos'].includes(route())){currentFilter='All';listQuery='';savedOnly=false;}render();});
document.addEventListener('click',e=>{let b=e.target.closest('[data-action]');if(!b)return;let {action,id,value}=b.dataset;
if(action==='install-app')installPortalApp();
if(action==='resource-link-edit')editResourceLink(id);
if(action==='resource-link-reset')resetResourceLinkForm();
if(action==='programme-edit')editProgramme(id);
if(action==='programme-reset')resetProgrammeForm();
if(action==='finance-clear')clearFinancePreview();
if(action==='community-toggle')toggleCommunityGroup(Number(id));
if(action==='social-edit')editSocialLink(Number(id));
if(action==='social-toggle')toggleSocialLink(Number(id));
if(action==='social-remove')removeSocialLink(Number(id));
if(action==='social-reset')resetSocialForm();
if(action==='reset-filters'){currentFilter='All';listQuery='';savedOnly=false;if(['notes','videos'].includes(route()))render();}
if(action==='download-note'){const n=allNotes().find(n=>n.id===id);if(n){const raw=document.createElement('div');raw.innerHTML=n.body;const blob=new Blob(['InspirED Institute\n'+n.title+'\n\nPrivate review note\n\n'+raw.innerText],{type:'text/plain;charset=utf-8'}),url=URL.createObjectURL(blob),a=document.createElement('a');a.href=url;a.download='InspirED-'+n.id+'.txt';a.click();setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(url),1000);}}
if(action==='clear-vocab-search'){$('#vocab-search').value='';$('#vocab-results').innerHTML=homophoneCards();$('#vocab-search').focus();}
if(action==='filter'){currentFilter=value;updateList();}
if(action==='saved-only'){savedOnly=!savedOnly;updateList();}
if(action==='bookmark'){let i=state.saved.indexOf(id);i<0?state.saved.push(id):state.saved.splice(i,1);save();render(true);toast(i<0?'Saved for your next revision.':'Removed from saved notes.');}
if(action==='complete-note'){if(!state.read.includes(id)){state.read.push(id);activity();}render(true);toast('One more step forward. Note completed!');}
if(action==='start-test')startTest(id);if(action==='sync-now')syncProgress(true);
if(['answer','previous','next','jump','flag','clear-answer'].includes(action)){let d=state.drafts[id];if(!d)return;let ix=d.index||0;if(action==='answer')d.answers[ix]=Number(value);if(action==='clear-answer')d.answers[ix]=null;if(action==='previous')d.index=Math.max(0,ix-1);if(action==='next')d.index=Math.min(TESTS.find(t=>t.id===id).questions.length-1,ix+1);if(action==='jump')d.index=Number(value);if(action==='flag'){let fi=d.flags.indexOf(ix);fi<0?d.flags.push(ix):d.flags.splice(fi,1);}save();render(true);}
if(action==='submit-dialog')confirmSubmit(id);if(action==='close-modal')$('#modal').close();if(action==='submit-test')submitTest(id);if(action==='review-attempt')go('result/'+id);
if(action==='load-video'){let v=VIDEOS.find(v=>v.id===id);$('#player').innerHTML=`<iframe class="video-frame" title="${esc(v.title)}" src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/${id}?autoplay=1" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe>`;}
if(action==='complete-video'){if(!state.watched.includes(id)){state.watched.push(id);activity();}b.disabled=true;b.innerHTML=icon('check')+'Completed';toast('Class completed. Your progress is updated.');}
});
function updateList(){let base=route().split('/')[0];document.querySelectorAll('[data-action="filter"]').forEach(b=>{b.classList.toggle('active',b.dataset.value===currentFilter);b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',b.dataset.value===currentFilter);});let sb=$('[data-action="saved-only"]');if(sb){sb.classList.toggle('active',savedOnly);sb.setAttribute('aria-pressed',savedOnly);}$('#resource-results').innerHTML=base==='notes'?noteResults():videoResults();}
document.addEventListener('input',e=>{if(e.target.id==='vocab-search'){$('#vocab-results').innerHTML=homophoneCards(e.target.value);}if(e.target.id==='filter-search'){listQuery=e.target.value;updateList();}});
document.addEventListener('change',e=>{if(e.target.id==='resource-link-kind')updateResourceChoices();if(e.target.id==='programme-kind')updateProgrammeParents();if(e.target.id==='goal'){state.goal=Number(e.target.value);save();toast('Weekly goal updated. Small steps count.');}});
document.addEventListener('submit',e=>{if(e.target.id==='resource-link-form'){e.preventDefault();saveResourceLink(e.target);return;}if(e.target.id==='programme-form'){e.preventDefault();saveProgramme(e.target);return;}if(e.target.id==='finance-preview-form'){e.preventDefault();previewFinance(e.target);return;}
if(e.target.id==='community-group-form'){e.preventDefault();saveCommunityGroup(e.target);return;}
if(e.target.id==='community-member-form'){e.preventDefault();saveCommunityMember(e.target);return;}
if(e.target.id==='social-link-form'){e.preventDefault();saveSocialLink(e.target);return;}
if(e.target.id==='global-search'||e.target.id==='page-search'){e.preventDefault();let q=e.target.querySelector('input').value.trim();go('search/'+encodeURIComponent(q));}
if(e.target.id==='profile-form'){e.preventDefault();const f=new FormData(e.target),name=f.get('name').trim();if(!name){$('#profile-error').textContent='Please enter a display name.';return;}state.profile={name,exam:f.get('exam')};save();go('home');toast('Your learning space is ready. Saving to your account.');}
if(e.target.id==='admin-note-form'){e.preventDefault();if(!isAdmin())return;let f=new FormData(e.target),title=f.get('title').trim(),body=f.get('body').trim();if(!title||!body){$('#admin-error').textContent='Add a title and note content.';return;}let n={id:'preview-note-'+Date.now(),title,category:f.get('category'),minutes:Math.max(1,Math.ceil(body.split(/\s+/).length/180)),description:'A review note added in the private Admin workspace.',letter:'N',body:body.split(/\n\s*\n/).map(p=>`<p>${esc(p).replace(/\n/g,'<br>')}</p>`).join('')};state.customNotes.push(n);save();go('notes/'+n.id);toast('Private note saved to your account.');}
});
render();
initCloud();
